B: Algebraic Number Theory
============================================================

B06: Discriminant of Q(ζ_6) = -3.0
  disc = -3 (the discriminant of x^2-x+1 = Φ_6(x))
  |disc| = 3 = n/phi(n) = 6/2 = sigma_-1(n)*phi(n) = ... 
  n/phi(6) = 3.0
  -3 = -(n/2). For n=6: -3. Is this special? No, disc(Q(ζ_n)) has formula for all n.
  sopfr(6)-2 = 3 = |disc| = 3? YES (5-2=3)
  BUT: Q(ζ_6)=Q(ζ_3), disc=-3 is from field Q(ζ_3), not specifically from 6.

B07: Q(sqrt(6)) fundamental unit: ε = 5 + 2√6
  Norm(ε) = 5² - 2²·6 = 25 - 24 = 1
  5 = sopfr(6) = 5 ✓
  2 = phi(6) = 2 ✓
  24 = J_2(6) (Jordan totient) = 6^2 * prod(1-1/p^2) for p|6
  J_2(6) = 6^2 * (3/4) * (8/9) = 24.0
  So Norm: sopfr(6)^2 - phi(6)^2 * 6 = 25 - 24 = 1
  The fundamental unit components ARE n=6 arithmetic functions!
  5 = sopfr(6), 2 = phi(6). Both specific to n=6. Non-trivial alignment.

B08: Regulator of Q(√6) = ln(5+2√6) = 2.292432
  vs GZ upper (0.5): 0.5000
  vs GZ center (1/e): 0.3679
  vs GZ width ln(4/3): 0.2877
  reg = 2.2924 >> all GZ constants
  reg / (2*pi) = 0.3649
  reg / sigma(6) = 0.1910
  2/reg = 0.8724
  reg ≈ 2.292. No clean GZ match.

B09: Signature of Q(ζ_6): (r1,r2) = (0,1)
  r2 = phi(6)/2 = 2/2 = 1
  r2=1 is the minimum possible complex place count for imaginary fields.
  phi(6)=2 is smallest possible Euler totient for n>2. Tautological consequence.
  True for Q(ζ_6)=Q(ζ_3): signature is always (0,1) for class of imaginary quadratic fields.

B10: Minkowski bound for Q(√-6)
  |disc(Q(sqrt(-6)))| = 24 (since -6 ≡ 2 mod 4)
  M = (2/2!) * (4/π)^1 * sqrt(24) = 1 * (4/π) * 4.8990
  M = 6.237574
  sigma(6) = 12
  M / sigma(6) = 0.5198
  M ≈ 6.238. sigma(6)=12. M/sigma = 0.5198.
  24 = J_2(6) = 24. Indeed |disc|=J_2(6)!
  M = (4/π)*sqrt(J_2(6)) = 6.2376
  Check: J_2(10)=72 vs 4*10=40. Not equal, so J_2(6)=4*6 is n=6 specific!

